From f0f46e9b4fdc7a7e6341ebfe5311cf006805e63e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PSRL <psrl@local>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 14:47:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] v0.29.0 patch

Narrow PSRL source patch for vLLM v0.29.0.

PSRL-specific changes:

- vllm/v1/metrics/stats.py: declare the PSRL SchedulerStats fields
  (req_id_to_prompt_token_num, req_id_to_response_token_num,
  preemption_req_ids). SchedulerStats travels from the EngineCore process to
  the API-server process inside the msgspec EngineCoreOutputs struct, so the
  frontend can only see fields that are declared on the class.
- vllm/v1/worker/gpu_model_runner.py: clamp the cached request block IDs to the
  block-table row capacity. A sync KV-load failure under the recompute policy
  truncates num_computed_tokens without going through the
  resumed_from_preemption replace path, while the runner only ever extends its
  own block IDs, so repeated rollbacks can overflow `append_row`.

Everything else in this patch is a verbatim backport of upstream commit
4ac452ad98 ("[Core] Release NCCL communicator memory in sleep mode",
PR #51485), which is merged upstream but postdates the v0.29.0 tag. It adds
ncclCommSuspend/ncclCommResume via pynccl_wrapper, PyNcclCommunicator
suspend/resume, parallel_state suspend_device_comms/resume_device_comms, and
the default-off ModelConfig.enable_nccl_comm_suspend flag, plus its tests.
Drop the backport once PSRL moves to a vLLM release that contains #51485.
